<p>
  <strong>Server side Filter Fields</strong>
</p>
<p>Only <strong>Active</strong>, in-date records are considered, ordered by <strong>Rule Prioritization Number ascending</strong> (lowest number on top), capped at 4000 rows. Records whose plant is Not Applicable or is the configured NPR/FAC default plant (Default_Plant_Location_For_NPR_AND_FAC) are excluded from this normal match.</p>
<ul>
  <li data-uuid="8674befc-8f13-4a59-bd13-19f630ee8c53">
    <strong>Bonded Zone Indicator</strong> - exact boolean match against the "Origin Bonded" selection in the UI (only shown for India/China addresses; defaults to Non-Bonded elsewhere).</li>
  <li data-uuid="0e9796c9-9118-4bdb-82f0-16b7ccb81049">
    <strong>Service Type</strong>
  </li>
  <li data-uuid="f05f58b9-9886-4d53-9ec6-843c943290d4">
    <strong>Remedy Type</strong>
  </li>
  <li data-uuid="8a41a55c-537b-4bfe-b015-273306c1f9c7">
    <strong>Sold To CMF</strong>
  </li>
  <li data-uuid="83c2c51a-4040-4efb-bba8-8cea8e4d6c54">
    <strong>Sales Organization</strong>
  </li>
  <li data-uuid="addce8f3-899e-45c7-adac-67e98e01abde">
    <strong>Country</strong> — Collection Address country for IMF freight, Return-to-Customer Address country for CRF freight.</li>
  <li data-uuid="d90943ca-41c7-461f-a28e-5143f1061628">
    <strong>Geography</strong>
  </li>
  <li data-uuid="144197f0-964d-4929-9286-cb63e461d5fa">
    <strong>Plant Type</strong> — only applied when supplied (optional refinement).</li>
</ul>
<p>The client takes the first record in the ordered result that has a non-blank Sales_Issue_Return_Location_Plant__c and uses its plant as the Return Location.</p>
<p>Note</p>
<p>If Remedy, Country, Service Type or the Bonded indicator aren't selected yet, the matrix isn't queried through the rule engine at all — instead a placeholder lookup returns whichever active Sales_Issue_Return_Location_Matrix record is flagged plant Not Applicable.</p>
<p>When Return Reason = <strong>Direct Return Repair</strong>, the normal matrix lookup is skipped entirely. R4C_AG_CollectionDetails_Controller.getCollectionDatahelper() instead fetches the repair site list and looks up the single active Return Location Matrix record for the org-wide NPR/FAC default plant (Default_Plant_Location_For_NPR_AND_FAC) directly, with no CMF/country filtering.</p>
<p>If the plant resolved by the matrix is MYF2 and the relevant country is Malaysia, the client calls R4C_AG_CollectionDetails_Controller.getMalaysiaDomesticPlant and substitutes its result as the Return Location instead — this is a client-side override applied after the matrix match, not a matrix filter.</p>
<p>No match found</p>
<p>If no record resolves a Return Location Plant, agents (non-Portal users) see a hard-stop error toast ("No Return Location") and cannot proceed until a matching rule exists.</p>
